CAMERA
25. Responsive Camera
Do not only resize the renderer.
Adapt the camera.
Suggested starting point:
if (isMobilePortrait) {
  camera.fov = 70;
  cameraOffset.set(0, 4.8, -11);
}

if (isMobileLandscape) {
  camera.fov = 62;
  cameraOffset.set(0, 3.7, -9);
}

if (isDesktop) {
  camera.fov = 58;
  cameraOffset.set(0, 3.5, -8.5);
}
Tune these values against the actual game coordinates.
Desktop
- cinematic chase view
- enough track ahead
Portrait
- farther behind
- slightly higher
- wider FOV
- ship around lower 30–35% of screen
Landscape
- slightly lower
- closer than portrait
- horizon around upper third
26. Orientation Change
Do not reload the race.
On orientation change:
1. detect new orientation
2. resize renderer
3. update camera aspect
4. update FOV
5. change HUD mode
6. reposition controls
7. preserve race state
const portrait =
  window.matchMedia("(orientation: portrait)").matches;
